      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwood%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The area around Greenwood served as a hunting ground for the Ojibwe, Menominee, and Ho-Chunk people before European settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwood%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Greenwood's Peace Memorial is a fifteen-foot sculpture created by artist Ernest Durig from concrete and fine white sand.",
